Authentication and Authorization are two different security concepts.
_________________________________________________________
Authentication is about verifying identity — who the user, service, or application is.
Authorization is about permissions — what actions that identity is allowed to perform on which resources.

In AWS, authentication is handled using IAM identities such as users, groups, and roles,
while authorization is controlled through IAM policies, resource-based policies, and Service Control Policies (SCPs).

In Azure, authentication is performed using Azure Active Directory (now Entra ID) for users, groups, and service principals, and 
authorization is enforced using Azure RBAC roles assigned at different scopes.

Authentication always happens first; authorization happens after identity is verified.
